program            = 006_builtin_functions
area               = 08_gcc_extensions
description        = GCC __builtin_* intrinsics restricted to deterministic target-independent results, folded and volatile-runtime variants
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_audit_flags     = -Wall -Wextra -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror
ub_notes           <<END
UB-GATE DEVIATION AND ITS REASON. Every program in area 08_gcc_extensions drops
-pedantic from the default warning gate. Reason: the constructs under test are
non-standard GCC extensions by definition, and -pedantic exists precisely to reject
them; retaining it would fail every program in the area for doing exactly what it is
meant to do. This is the only area-wide deviation in the corpus. No other warning is
relaxed: -Wall, -Wextra, -Wconversion, -Wsign-conversion, -Wshadow and -Werror are all
retained, and this program is clean under them at -O0, -O1 and -O2. Measured with
gcc 13.3.0.

UB-FREEDOM ARGUMENT. There is no signed overflow: the only signed values are -12345 and
small counts, and __builtin_abs is applied to -12345, which is far from INT_MIN, so the
absolute value is representable. All bit manipulation is on unsigned types, where
wraparound is modular and defined.

Every shift count is strictly in range: the only shift is 1ULL << 40, and 40 is less than
the 64-bit width of unsigned long long on every target.

EVERY clz AND ctz ARGUMENT IS STRICTLY NON-ZERO, because __builtin_clz(0), __builtin_ctz(0),
__builtin_clzll(0) and __builtin_ctzll(0) are UNDEFINED. The arguments used are the
literals 1u, 0x80000000u, 8u, 1ULL and 1ULL << 40, and at run time the volatile value
0xF0F0F0F0, all provably non-zero.

NO UNINITIALIZED READ OCCURS. __builtin_memset zeroes all 16 bytes of dst before
__builtin_memcpy writes the first 8, so reading dst[8] and dst[15] is well defined; src is
fully written by its loop before it is read. The memcpy copies exactly 8 bytes from an
8-byte source into a 16-byte destination, so no one-past-end access occurs. The sanitizer
gate confirms both.

There is no aliasing violation: the char arrays are accessed only as char, and every other
object only through its declared type. No object is modified twice between sequence points.
Every printf call receives at most one side-effecting argument. Nothing depends on padding
bytes: the program prints offsetof values, which are specified, and never reads the padding
they imply. Nothing depends on the addresses of unrelated objects, and no address is
printed.

No char value is ever printed. char was measured as signed on x86_64 and i686 but unsigned
on aarch64 and riscv64; the char arrays here are only compared byte-wise or tested against
zero, so the signedness difference cannot be observed.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Nothing implementation-defined is observed, so no target restriction is needed and all
four targets are compared. Achieving that required three deliberate exclusions and one
normalization.

EXCLUDED: __builtin_constant_p. Its result reflects the OPTIMIZER'S decisions and so
legitimately differs between -O0 and -O2. Including it would break this program's own
optimization-invariance requirement and produce a divergence caused by the test.

EXCLUDED: __builtin_return_address, __builtin_frame_address, __builtin_FILE,
__builtin_LINE, __builtin_trap, __builtin_unreachable, __builtin_alloca. Addresses and
file paths are not deterministic across builds or targets, and trap and unreachable
deliberately produce undefined or abnormal termination, which would destroy the UB-freedom
precondition that makes the oracle sound.

EXCLUDED: every l-suffixed bit builtin such as __builtin_popcountl, __builtin_clzl and
__builtin_ctzl. They take unsigned long, which is 32-bit on i686 and 64-bit on the other
three targets, so __builtin_clzl(1ul) would print 31 on i686 and 63 elsewhere. Only
unsuffixed forms, which take 32-bit unsigned int, and ll-suffixed forms, which take 64-bit
unsigned long long, are used; both are fixed-width on every target.

NORMALIZED: the __builtin_strcmp results. Only the SIGN of a strcmp result is specified;
its magnitude is implementation-defined. Each result is reduced to exactly -1, 0 or 1
before printing.

bi_offsetof is target-independent by careful member ordering. In struct off_s { int x;
int y; double z; } the two ints already place z at offset 8, and 8 is a multiple of BOTH 4,
which is i686's default struct alignment for double with -malign-double off, AND 8, which
is the alignment on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64. So z lands at offset 8 on every target
with no padding inserted before it. Reordering these members, for instance putting the
double first or a single int before it, would expose the i686 versus LP64 double-alignment
difference and manufacture a divergence.

Cast discipline for the strict gate: bswap16 and bswap32 results are cast to unsigned,
bswap64 to unsigned long long, strlen and offsetof to unsigned because they return size_t
whose width varies, and __builtin_expect to int because it takes and returns long, where
the value 5 fits on every target including i686.

The __builtin_ forms of memset, memcpy, memcmp, strcmp, strlen and offsetof are used
rather than the library names precisely because they REQUIRE NO HEADER, and the corpus
includes none.

The builtin selection deliberately favours the most universally-implemented, deterministic
builtins over exotic coverage, because the documentation supports __builtin_* only
generically at docs/technical-specifications.md lines 13, 107 and 761 and
docs/project-guide.md lines 81 and 206, with no enumerated list of individual builtins
anywhere. Breadth of safety was preferred so that one unimplemented builtin cannot block
the program. Because no documentation enumerates individual builtins, there is no
documented basis to cite and this program carries NO expected-divergence marker: an
unimplemented builtin would be an undocumented divergence and therefore a FINDING.

Output is identical on all four targets at all three optimization levels.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
bi_popcount32=16
bi_popcount64=13
bi_clz_one=31
bi_clz_top=0
bi_ctz_eight=3
bi_clzll_one=63
bi_ctzll_bit40=40
bi_bswap16=13330
bi_bswap32=1144201745
bi_bswap64=578437695752307201
bi_abs=12345
bi_strlen=11
bi_strcmp_sign=-1 1 0
bi_mem_roundtrip=1
bi_offsetof=0 4 8
bi_expect_taken=7
bi_expect_value=5
bi_runtime_popcount32=16
bi_runtime_popcount64=13
bi_runtime_clz=0
bi_runtime_ctz=4
bi_runtime_bswap32=4042322160
bi_runtime_abs=12345
END
